<BaseLayout
  title="About — Portfolio Lab"
  description="Portfolio Lab is a free, browser-only portfolio studio for Indian investors. No sign-up, no data leaves your device."
>
  <div class="spine page-head">
    <h1>About</h1>
    <p class="lede">Free portfolio studio for Indian investors — browser-only, no account required.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="prose-spine prose">
    <p class="lede">
      Portfolio Lab is a tool to help you design a max-Sharpe portfolio with an honest downside
      layer. All computation is client-side. Nothing is sent to any server.
    </p>

    <h2>What it does</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Guides you through a 14-question risk profile questionnaire.</li>
      <li>Runs a max-Sharpe optimizer over 9 Indian-market asset classes.</li>
      <li>Lets you override weights manually and recomputes Sharpe live.</li>
      <li>Projects bear / base / bull scenario bands and a 1,000-path Monte Carlo cone.</li>
      <li>Flags every asset below the 12% forward-return floor in red with sourced caveats.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>What it doesn't do</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Not a robo-advisor. No account. No KYC. No order execution.</li>
      <li>Does not store your data anywhere — not even a database on the server.</li>
      <li>Does not make buy/sell recommendations. It shows math, not mandates.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Built by</h2>
    <p>
      <a href="https://oriz.in">Chirag Singhal</a> — part of the
      <a href="https://oriz.in">oriz</a> family of free financial tools for India.
    </p>
    <p>
      Source data: Value Research, Vanguard VCMM, RBI, LBMA, ICICIdirect.
      See <a href="/methodology/">methodology</a> for full sourcing.
    </p>

    <hr />

